{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"saturationLargestFirst"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"DSatur (Brélaz 1979): first a vertex of greatest degree, then repeatedly the uncoloured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with the most distinct colours among its neighbours, ties to the greatest degree in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the whole graph, then to the lesser index. Exact on bipartite graphs. O((n + m) log n)."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/saturationlargestfirst"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.saturationLargestFirst","symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"saturationLargestFirst"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/Coloring.swift#L120","fileName":"Coloring.swift"},"externalID":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO22saturationLargestFirstyA2CmF","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case"},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/saturationLargestFirst":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","abstract":[{"text":"DSatur (Brélaz 1979): first a v